eferences.md", ".prawduct/changes/solve-policy.md", ".prawduct/operator-verification.md", "CHANGELOG.md", "src/Cordyceps.Tests/SolvePolicyTests.cs", "src/Cordyceps.Tests/SolveWaitTests.cs", "src/Cordyceps.Tests/SolverStateTests.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/SolveCoordinator.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/SolvePolicy.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Core/SolverState.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Knowledge/BestPracticesGuide.md", "src/Cordyceps/Knowledge/CommonErrorsGuide.md", "src/Cordyceps/Knowledge/GettingStartedGuide.md", "src/Cordyceps/Knowledge/Prompts/CreateParametricGeometry.md", "src/Cordyceps/Knowledge/Prompts/PlanDefinition.md", "src/Cordyceps/McpServer.cs", "src/Cordyceps/Tools/Unified/GhDocumentTool.cs"], "files_oracle": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-solve-policy.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md", ".prawduct/changes/solve-policy.md", ".prawduct/operator-verification.md", ".prawduct/owner-rulings.md"], "findings": [], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 0, "note": 0}, "observations": [{"goal": "Nothing Is Unintended", "title": "Which actions read timeout is decided in the host file, untested", "recommendation": "Instance. The R-4/R-7 fix made solver (enabled=true) and revert read and validate timeout. The choice of which actions do that is the new private static GhDocumentTool.WaitsForSolve. It sits in a host-coupled file and no test covers it, although CLAUDE.md and the core learnings rule say decision logic like this goes in a host-free Core/ file with tests. The rest is covered: the parse (TryParseTimeout) and the reply (WaitedReply) are both tested, and the predicate is three lines anyone can read. If the builder wants this fixed, move the predicate into SolvePolicy with an InlineData theory (recompute, revert and solver true read timeout; solver false, clear and info do not) in a commit that is already planned. Nothing needs a disposition.", "about": {"review_id": "rev-20261111T173627Z-310b33f7", "fid": "R-7"}, "oid": "O-1"}], "duration_seconds": 420, "scope": "sol